LOK: Impress applies queued pane changes before a command

Impress queues pane reconfiguration in user events. A LOK command that
arrives first finds the slide sorter shell off the dispatcher stack, and
slots it serves (hide, show) are dropped without a trace. A new
ITiledRenderable::settleViews runs before dispatch; Impress drains its
configuration queue there.

